# Dragon's Lair (USA).cue -- drive the attract movie into gameplay and die,
# forcing a scene BRANCH (a near-full-stroke seek to the death clip and back).
#
# HLE boot mode (core default: virtualjaguar_cd_boot_mode=hle).
# For the real-BIOS path use dragons_lair_death_branch_bios.press -- BIOS boot
# is +439 fields, and `--bios` alone does NOT switch CD boot mode; that needs
# --option virtualjaguar_cd_boot_mode=bios.
#
# Verified on libretro/develop @ 674f600 -- see docs/fmv-drift-notes.md §10.
#
# Timeline (fields, absolute from boot, HLE):
#   ~500/560  pause x2 leaves the attract loop and starts a game
#   ~700      `a` is the first QTE input; the branch fires the same field
#   ~700      BRANCH: CD read jumps LBA 16026 -> 154061 (+138035 sectors)
#   ~828      BRANCH: LBA 154061 -> 20491 (retry scene)
#   thereafter the die/retry loop self-repeats every ~1171 fields with no
#   further input: branches at ~1871, ~2000, ~3043, ~3172, ...
#
# Success criterion (objective, not visual): a CD read whose LBA delta from
# the previous read exceeds 100000 sectors.  Steady-state streaming reads step
# 339-428 sectors and the attract-loop restart steps 5171, so the separation is
# ~2.5 orders of magnitude.  A no-press control run produces NO such jump.
#
#   bash test/tools/run_dl_branch_fixture.sh ./virtualjaguar_libretro.dylib
#
# NOTE for HLE runs: the `seeks`/`seekstarts`/`seekdones` columns of
# fmv_seek_probe's CSV are incremented only by the BUTCH $12xx register path in
# src/cd/cdrom.c, which HLE bypasses entirely.  They are structurally 0 in HLE
# whether or not a branch happened -- do not use them as the HLE gate.  Use the
# HLE_READ trace event's LBA instead (VJ_CD_TRACE=1 VJ_CD_TRACE_LIVE=1).

500:pause
560:pause
700:a
